31,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Oh no! I found out that the outer wards lost their buses! And the roads north of the river close so often in winter. We can't rely on transport!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Fascinating. My research shows we've tried outreach before with great success in the outer wards, yet we let it die. We are repeating a cycle of abandonment.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The problem isn't the cycle; it's the competence. We have no one on the payroll qualified to supervise new facilitators, and our tool certification has lapsed.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The financial data confirms my fears. The grant is a one-year spike. If we choose a service with high recurring vehicle costs, we will be bankrupt by year two.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I saw the bus links are gone. People in the outer wards are really cut off now. If we only keep things at the main branch, they can't reach us.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, that's exactly what I'm worried about! If we use a mobile library but the roads close or the budget for gas disappears, we're just letting people down again!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the data from six years ago proves the demand is there. The failure wasn't the idea; it was the lack of institutional memory. We must not let ""budget spikes"" dictate our vision.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Vision is a luxury for those who can actually manage the work. If we launch a technical or tool-based service, we have no one to certify the equipment. It's a liability.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, vision without a sustainable budget is just a fantasy. If we commit to a high-maintenance mobile service, we will be forced to cut it mid-way through the second year.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"But... if we don't go to them, they just... they can't come. The bus rerouting makes it almost impossible for some. We have to find a way.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"Maybe we can find a way that doesn't depend on the roads or the buses? Like something that stays in the community halls? @Daisuke, wouldn't that be better?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. The partner-run groups from six years ago survived because they were embedded in the community, not dependent on a library van. We should look for a ""stationary-remote"" model.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Even in community halls, you need a supervisor. My findings show our staff are already stretched thin and lack the specific training to manage remote sites. We are just adding more to their plates.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shion is correct about the staffing, but @Benjamin's point about the budget is key. A stationary model reduces the vehicle running costs that plagued last year's budget.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think I agree. If we use the halls, the road closures won't stop the people who already live there from getting the service.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,Yay! I'm so glad we're thinking about this! We need a plan that stays strong even when the weather is bad or the buses change!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a rare pleasure to see logic prevail over the desire for a ""shiny"" new mobile unit. Let us hope the candidates reflect this stability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I remain skeptical. No matter the location, if the skill set isn't on the roster, the staff will simply burn out trying to fake it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"We will evaluate the candidates based on three criteria: low recurring vehicle costs, minimal need for specialized supervision, and accessibility for the outer wards.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I just... I hope we can actually help the people who are cut off. That's all I really want.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
