60,3,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I really don't like Option D! The road closures and the bus issues mean it's too risky. Option C sounds lovely and uses partners, which is much safer!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option D is a ghost of the past—high demand, but doomed by the very logistics @Yumi mentioned. Option C mirrors the successful partner-run groups I found in the records.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is a disaster. We have no one to certify the tools. Option D is a logistical nightmare. Option B is the only one that doesn't require a physical supervisor on-site.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option D is financially irresponsible. The vehicle running costs would create a deficit by the second year. Option A also requires high equipment maintenance. Option C is the most sustainable.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Option D... it sounds like it helps the most people, but if the roads close, they're still left out. Option C... if it's in the community halls, they can reach it.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, but Option B is just a website! It doesn't help the people who are lonely or cut off in the outer wards. Option C brings people together!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shion, while Option B is safe, it is sterile. Option C leverages the community's own strength, which is exactly why the programs from six years ago survived. It is the logical choice.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Yumi, ""bringing people together"" is a sentiment, not a strategy. Option C requires coordination and supervision of facilitators. We've already established our staff cannot handle more commitments.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, Option C uses ""partner community organizations."" This shifts the supervisory burden away from our internal staff and onto the partners, mitigating the staffing risk.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,If the partners do the supervising... then it's okay? I think Option C is the best way to reach the people who can't get to the main branch.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"Exactly! It's a win-win! It's friendly, it's stable, and it doesn't care if the buses are rerouted because it's already there in the neighborhood!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is the only option that respects both the historical data of what works and the current logistical constraints. I find it quite elegant in its simplicity.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"I still find the reliance on ""partners"" to be a gamble, but compared to the liability of uncertified tools in Option A or the budget hole of Option D, it is the least offensive.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"From a financial perspective, Option C is the only one that avoids the ""second-year crash."" It uses existing community infrastructure rather than creating new, expensive overhead.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel okay with Option C. It's the only one that really feels like it's reaching out to the people who are forgotten.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we all agree! Let's make this happen for everyone!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare moment of consensus. I shall cast my vote for the option that avoids the mistakes of our predecessors.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"I will vote for it, though I expect the staff will still complain about the coordination. It is simply the most logical of the flawed choices.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,The decision is clear. Option C provides the necessary reach without compromising the long-term financial health of the library system.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,Me too... I'll vote for C.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
